# Defensive Security Intro

## Overview

This room introduces the fundamentals of defensive security and explains how security professionals protect systems, networks, and data from cyber threats.

## Objectives

- Understand what defensive security is.
- Learn the role of defensive security professionals.
- Explore how organizations detect and respond to threats.
- Complete the practical challenge.

## Skills Learned

- Defensive Security fundamentals
- Security monitoring concepts
- Threat detection basics
- Incident response introduction
- Blue Team mindset

## Tools Used

- TryHackMe AttackBox
- Web Browser

## Key Takeaways

- Defensive security focuses on protecting systems and reducing security risks.
- Security teams use monitoring and analysis to detect suspicious activities.
- Incident response helps organizations handle and recover from cyber attacks.
- A strong defense requires continuous improvement and security awareness.

## Reflection

This room introduced me to the defensive side of cybersecurity.
It helped me understand how security teams protect organizations,monitor threats,and respond to incidents.
Learning both offensive and defensive security provides a better understanding of how cybersecurity works as a whole.
I found myself more interested in the offensive side of cybersecurity and penetration testing. 
Understanding how defenders detect and respond to attacks will help me become a better penetration tester by providing insight into security controls and defensive strategies.

